  - [1mSeed data:[0m [38;5;153mseed(n=237)[39m goes through [38;5;153mcreateTask[39m, so seeded ids are 1–237. Every 3 tasks share a [38;5;153mcreatedAt[39m value (base
    + floor(i/3) minutes).
  - [1mPaging:[0m ids are unique and always increasing, but [38;5;153mcreatedAt[39m repeats. A cursor on [38;5;153mcreatedAt[39m alone would skip or
    repeat rows. Using [38;5;153m(createdAt, id)[39m or [38;5;153mid[39m alone would be stable. The file header says the store stands in for a
    Postgres table with about 4M rows taking about 30 inserts/sec.

